title: Renaissance — DAG integrity validator (first governance-backlog item, T-007)
summary: 'Built the first task-governance backlog item: validateTaskDag() in task-loader, the graph integrity check nothing owned before (assertTransition validated status, never the graph). Detects self-parent, dangling parentTaskId/dependsOn, and cycles via iterative DFS over parent ∪ dependsOn edges (each cycle once, diamonds safe). Cid surfaces violations on the captain board as an advise-only integrity[] field — never auto-edits, never blocks, per the governance decision. +7 tests; MCP 445 / CLI 441 green; board smoke-tested (integrity absent = sound graph). Done while a team review of the shipped Tasks section runs in the background.'
