learnings:
  - 'Wiring T-011 (aggregate-on-settle) revealed an architecture snag worth flagging: the calibrate AGGREGATION lives in the CLI package while settlement lives in MCP, and MCP can''t import from CLI — which is exactly WHY aggregation never ran automatically. T-011 needs an extraction refactor first (move aggregation MCP-ward). Pivoted to T-007 (self-contained) instead.'
  - 'The DAG validator follows the governance ownership cleanly: it LIVES in task-loader (the framework chokepoint) but Cid INVOKES it at board-assemble — the present-tense owner surfaces present-tense structural defects, advise-only. Ownership = who invokes + surfaces, not just where the code sits.'
